From: cbodotnet maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Use the SDK under test to create its HTTPS developer certificate

The pinned preview global tool is unavailable on the current official feeds,
and its historical service index returns HTTP 403. Use the fresh SDK's built-in
dev-certs command for the same certificate setup. Keep every HTTPS test and
assertion. The test preparation records the tool assembly and its local source
package identity before this test-only patch is applied.

diff --git a/smoke-test.sh b/smoke-test.sh
--- a/smoke-test.sh
+++ b/smoke-test.sh
@@ -284,12 +284,11 @@
 }
 
 function setupDevCerts() {
-    echo "Setting up dotnet-dev-certs $devCertsVersion to generate dev certificate" | tee -a "$logFile"
+    echo "Using the SDK built-in dotnet dev-certs to generate the HTTPS developer certificate" | tee -a "$logFile"
     (
         set -x
-        "$dotnetDir/dotnet" tool install -g dotnet-dev-certs --version "$devCertsVersion" --add-source https://dotnetfeed.blob.core.windows.net/dotnet-core/index.json
         export DOTNET_ROOT="$dotnetDir"
-        "$testingHome/.dotnet/tools/dotnet-dev-certs" https
+        "$dotnetDir/dotnet" dev-certs https
     ) >> "$logFile" 2>&1
 }
 
